<title>JAPAN: MOTOR RACING-AKAI TO SPONSOR BENETTON FORMULA ONE TEAM.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-AKAI TO SPONSOR BENETTON FORMULA ONE TEAM.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Akai Electric Co Ltd, a Tokyo-based audio equipment maker, said on Monday it had agreed to sponsor the Benetton Formula One team in the 1997 and 1998 seasons.</p>
<p>The company have an option to extend the contract to 1999, an Akai spokesman said.</p>
<p>Akai did not disclose the cost of the deal.</p>
<p>Austrian Gerhard Berger finished fourth in his Benetton in the season-opening Australian Grand Prix on Sunday in a race won by Britain's David Coulthard driving a McLaren.</p>
</text>
